WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.770 --> 00:00:05.470
David, how likely is it that Donald Trump
will declare martial law at some point in

00:00:05.470 --> 00:00:11.799
his presidency, either to avoid being impeached
and removed, or if he loses in 2020 to avoid

00:00:11.799 --> 00:00:18.020
relinquishing the white house or in advance
of the 2020 election to justify not having

00:00:18.020 --> 00:00:19.070
the election altogether?

00:00:19.070 --> 00:00:25.360
All right, so three different scenarios where
the, this, uh, emailer wonders if Donald Trump

00:00:25.360 --> 00:00:27.610
will apply martial law.

00:00:27.610 --> 00:00:28.610
Declare martial law.

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:29.610
Here's the reality.

00:00:29.610 --> 00:00:30.650
It's extremely unlikely.

00:00:30.650 --> 00:00:31.840
It is extremely.

00:00:31.840 --> 00:00:38.230
So martial law is a suspension effectively
of the normal law enforcement infrastructure

00:00:38.230 --> 00:00:44.450
of the country replaced by the military, taking
control of domestic law enforcement.

00:00:44.450 --> 00:00:49.770
Now, on a federal level, only the president
has the power to impose martial law.

00:00:49.770 --> 00:00:55.630
And this all goes back to, um, uh, limitations
on martial law that exists thanks to court

00:00:55.630 --> 00:01:00.530
decisions, which were established between
the civil war and world war II.

00:01:00.530 --> 00:01:07.679
So for example, in 1878, Congress passed the
posse Comitatus act, which forbids military

00:01:07.679 --> 00:01:11.969
involvement in domestic law enforcement without
congressional approval.

00:01:11.969 --> 00:01:15.759
And that ultimately may be what is the deciding
factor here?

00:01:15.759 --> 00:01:20.889
Even if we attribute absolutely the worst
intentions to Donald Trump, which include

00:01:20.889 --> 00:01:27.149
that in an act of desperation where he's about
to get convicted on impeachment or he's about

00:01:27.149 --> 00:01:31.670
to lose the election or he has lost the election
and it's almost time for him to go.

00:01:31.670 --> 00:01:37.040
The idea is in an act of desperation, he will
declare martial law strictly speaking, you

00:01:37.040 --> 00:01:43.549
need congressional approval in order to, uh,
declare martial law based on, uh, the posse

00:01:43.549 --> 00:01:45.090
Comitatus act.

00:01:45.090 --> 00:01:51.479
So I think the better question is, would Trump
try to put in place martial law?

00:01:51.479 --> 00:01:57.340
Maybe, although I still doubt it, but if he
did, who is in control of the house and Senate

00:01:57.340 --> 00:01:59.979
at the time and would they allow it?

00:01:59.979 --> 00:02:04.840
And this is why, once again, you know, we
talk about the 2018 midterms and Democrats

00:02:04.840 --> 00:02:06.719
taking over control of the house.

00:02:06.719 --> 00:02:09.820
Now they have the investigative power of the
house.

00:02:09.820 --> 00:02:11.660
Now we have impeachment hearings.

00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:15.930
Now we are potentially heading in the direction
of a trial of an impeachment trial.

00:02:15.930 --> 00:02:18.190
Uh, this is why this stuff matters.

00:02:18.190 --> 00:02:22.371
And this is why taking over the Senate and
although it's an uphill battle in 2020 or

00:02:22.371 --> 00:02:24.950
maybe in 2022, that's why this stuff really
matters.

00:02:24.950 --> 00:02:30.790
I believe that there is no question Donald
Trump will make the case that because of some

00:02:30.790 --> 00:02:36.510
unfair treatment either, uh, in the context
of the impeachment inquiry or the election

00:02:36.510 --> 00:02:41.320
or whatever, Trump will make the case that
he didn't really lose or that someone cheated

00:02:41.320 --> 00:02:43.400
or that this was rigged or this, that that
was regular.

00:02:43.400 --> 00:02:48.290
The other thing, I think it is less likely
that he will actually try to declare martial

00:02:48.290 --> 00:02:54.630
law and I think it is almost an impossibility
that he would be able to get away with it.

00:02:54.630 --> 00:02:57.250
But things have happened for the first time
before.

00:02:57.250 --> 00:03:00.320
I mean, think about other times martial law
has been declared in the United States is

00:03:00.320 --> 00:03:01.320
very limited.

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:05.500
I think after Pearl Harbor was bombed, martial
law was declared.

00:03:05.500 --> 00:03:10.540
Uh, and uh, if I have my history correct,
I almost don't want to say, but I think that

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:14.000
that was related to the internment camps of
Japanese Americans.

00:03:14.000 --> 00:03:18.940
Um, but the instances in which martial law
was, was declared are extraordinarily limited.

00:03:18.940 --> 00:03:22.140
And the idea that a house and Senate would
allow, particularly when not controlled by

00:03:22.140 --> 00:03:26.040
Trump's party, that the house and Senate would
allow Trump to declare martial law because

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:28.580
he thinks the election against him was unfair.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:31.200
Um, that the election that went against him
was unfair.

00:03:31.200 --> 00:03:33.579
It seems extremely unlikely, but I'm willing
to have my mind changed.

